refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public voidTime\Duration::__unserialize arraydata
Restores a Time\Duration object from the data produced by serialize. This method is called by unserialize and is not meant to be called directly.

&reftitle.parameters;
data
An array with the seconds, nanoseconds and negative elements, corresponding to the properties of the class.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Serializing and unserializing a Time\Duration


<?php
$serialized = serialize(Time\Duration::fromSeconds(1, 2)->negate());
var_dump($serialized);

var_dump(unserialize($serialized));

try {
    unserialize('O:13:"Time\Duration":3:{s:7:"seconds";i:0;s:11:"nanoseconds";i:1000000000;s:8:"negative";b:0;}');
} catch (Exception $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


   &example.outputs;


